        "evidence": "trefoil-knot-group.md:11-14 'This relation xyx=yxy is the braid relation: it encodes the fact that the three-strand braid may be closed into the trefoil by identifying the top and bottom of the braid.'",
        "notes": "The trefoil is the closure of the 2-braid σ_1^3 (a 2-strand closure), not naturally 'the closure of the three-strand braid'. The isomorphism π_1≅B_3 is correct, but the causal gloss ('closed into the trefoil by identifying top and bottom of the [three-strand] braid') conflates the B_3 group isomorphism with the geometric closure, which for the trefoil is a 2-strand operation. Minor expository imprecision in a remark."
